PG  - 175
AB  - Radical prostatectomy is a standard treatment option for many patients with 
      clinically localized prostate cancer; however, little information about its 
      safety and efficacy is available to help guide patients who have undergone prior 
      organ transplantation. We present 2 cases of patients with prior hepatic 
      transplantation who each subsequently underwent radical prostatectomy. In each 
      case, the prostate tumor was organ confined, and both patients were biochemically 
      free of disease at last follow-up.
