      hepatobiliary surgery].
PG  - 316-320
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.issn.0529-5815.2017.04.016 [doi]
AB  - Hepatobiliary surgery is considered to be technically challenging because of 
      complex intrahepatic and perihilar anatomical structures and variations.Nowadays, 
      three-dimensional imaging technique plays an important role in the time of 
      precise liver surgery.Three-dimensional images depict the spatial location of 
      tumor, and the course, confluence pattern and variation of portal vein, hepatic 
      artery, biliary system and hepatic vein distinctly while showing involved hepatic 
      segments and the relationship with adjacent vessels from omnidirectional view, 
      measuring the length of margin and future remnant liver.With the help of surgical 
      simulation, surgeons can determine the significant vessels preoperatively.The 
      application of three-dimensional imaging technique may improve the resectability 
      and safety of complex hepatobiliary surgery, such as hilar cholangiocarcinoma, 
      centrally located liver tumor, hepatolithiasis and living donor liver 
      transplantation.Meanwhile, three-dimensional visualization facilitates the 
      understanding of two-dimensional images and complicated surgical anatomy for 
      surgeons.
